// Single source of truth for the `exportClones` memory request.
//
//     ram = clamp(perByte x size("clns"), floorGiB, 128 GiB)
//
// exportClones reads the complete CloneSet into heap. A constant value cannot size it.
// A single-cell export then builds a second, expanded list with divideClonesByTags. That
// list holds one clone for each (clonotype x cell) pair. A single-cell export therefore
// uses a higher floor and a steeper slope than a bulk export. The --chains option filters
// only after the expansion. An export of one chain group still costs the complete file.
//
// The floor sizes a small input, where the in-heap tag-count graph is larger than the
// stored file. The linear term sizes a large input. size("clns") is the stored blob size.
// The SDK reads the blob size from metadata and runs no pre-exec pass. On a backend that
// does not supply blob size, the formula uses its static fallback, which is the floor.
//
// The mixcr entrypoint computes the heap limits from the container grant R:
//     -Xmx = max(min(0.85*R, R - 3500 MiB), 0.5*R)
//     -Xms = 0.5*R
// The 3500 MiB non-heap reserve is constant, so it costs a small grant more than a large
// one. A 12 GiB grant gives 8788 MiB of heap. That heap failed on a 10.7k-cell /
// 26.7k-clone 10x BCR sample. A 5 GiB grant gives 2560 MiB. A 24 GiB grant gives
// 20889 MiB, which is 2.4x the heap that failed.
//
// Keep the floors low. -Xms is half the grant, so the backend reserves the full request
// at start. One sample runs one bulk export and one single-cell export for each chain
// group, and these run at the same time. An over-estimate does not only reserve the
// memory. The JVM also touches it.
//
// The Advanced Settings override replaces the linear term. It does not replace the floor.
// That setting is a whole-analysis number and also sizes `mixcr analyze`. A value below
// the floor gives the export less memory than exportClones needs.

exec := import("@platforma-sdk/workflow-tengo:exec")

f := exec.formula

// CAP_GIB is the upper bound of the formula. It does not bound the override.
CAP_GIB := 128

// Per-export floors. Read the -Xms note above before you change these values.
BULK_FLOOR_GIB := 16
BULK_PER_BYTE := 16
SINGLE_CELL_FLOOR_GIB := 24
SINGLE_CELL_PER_BYTE := 32

// exportRam returns the value for `.resources({onCPU:{ram}})`. It returns a size string
// when the caller supplies overrideGiB. It returns an exec.formula node when overrideGiB
// is undefined.
exportRam := func(floorGiB, perByte, overrideGiB) {
	if !is_undefined(overrideGiB) {
		if overrideGiB < floorGiB {
			overrideGiB = floorGiB
		}
		return string(overrideGiB) + "GiB"
	}
	return f.size("clns").times(perByte).
		between(f.gib(floorGiB), f.gib(CAP_GIB)).
		staticFallback(f.gib(floorGiB))
}

export {
	CAP_GIB: CAP_GIB,
	BULK_FLOOR_GIB: BULK_FLOOR_GIB,
	BULK_PER_BYTE: BULK_PER_BYTE,
	SINGLE_CELL_FLOOR_GIB: SINGLE_CELL_FLOOR_GIB,
	SINGLE_CELL_PER_BYTE: SINGLE_CELL_PER_BYTE,
	exportRam: exportRam
}
